# Layer A form: clock-derived audit path written via the
# Filesystem.Write stub inside a CAP narrowed to exactly the body's
# effect closure {writeFx, nowFx}; program adds 7 -> 7. Deriving the
# path reads the clock INSIDE the scope, so narrowing to [writeFx]
# alone trips CapabilityScopeUnsatisfiable. Uses prelude writeFx/
# nowFx/now/intToStr/concat/add/stringT/intT; the stub FN and
# literals are explicit.
@v=1 root=app
writeT FNT [stringT] intT [writeFx]
write FN "strand-builtin:Filesystem.Write" writeT [writeFx]
callNow APP now []
ts APP intToStr [callNow]
prefix STR "audit-"
logPath APP concat [prefix ts]
writeCall APP write [logPath]
scoped CAP [writeFx nowFx] writeCall
seven ILT 7
app APP add [scoped seven]
